00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:11.669 align:start position:0%
on february 27th at approximately  midnight a night county sheriff's office  deputy was involved in a fight with a  suspect outside of shenanigan's bar in  param without backup the deputy was  initially parked in the parking lot of  shenanigans on calvada boulevard a man  approached the deputy at his driver's  side window and pointed at him while  recording with his cell phone  the man later identified as joshua  briscoe age 42 of pahrump began asking  the deputy why he was parked there  when the deputy exited his patrol car to  ask if he needed help briscoe continued  cursing and asking why he was parked  there the deputy walked into the bar to  locate security and briscoe followed him  the deputy had to tell briscoe to back  up and physically push him back for both  of their safety as the deputy was  exiting the bar briscoe approached him  from behind in a threatening manner the  deputy attempted to detain briscoe and  he began to physically resist by hitting  kicking and grabbing the deputy's arms  and legs while the deputy was attempting  to restrain briscoe a second male jumped  onto the deputy's back and wrapped his  arm around his neck and began to choke  him  he fled the scene shortly after briscoe  was eventually restrained and placed  under arrest he was booked into the ny  county detention center for battery on a  protected person  anyone with information on the identity  of the second suspect seen in this video  is urged to contact the nye county  sheriff's office at 775-751-7000  or by email at sheriff co.nye.nv.us  [Music]  you
 

